; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Backwards Talk
; CATEGORY: Words & Text
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     recursion, reverse, words, sentences, lput
; SUMMARY:  Reverses letters, words and whole sentences three different ways with small recursive procedures.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Takes a sentence and prints it backwards in three ways:
;     1. the words in reverse order    (dog lazy the)
;     2. every word spelled backwards  (eht yzal god)
;     3. both at once, like a mirror   (god yzal eht)
;   Then it asks you for sentences of your own.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. When asked, type a sentence and press Enter.
;   Type quit or just press Enter to stop.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * recursion on a word: last letter first, then the rest
;   * recursion on a list: the same idea with SENTENCE instead of WORD
;   * how words and lists are alike in Logo (FIRST, BUTFIRST, LAST
;     and BUTLAST work on both)
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Logo has a REVERSE primitive. Check that it agrees with BACKWORD
;   * Write SWAPENDS that swaps only the first and last letters
;   * Print just the words that read the same forwards and backwards
; ============================================================

; Spell one word backwards. The last letter goes first, followed by
; the rest of the word (BUTLAST) spelled backwards.
to backword :wd
  if emptyp :wd [output "]
  output word last :wd backword butlast :wd
end

; Exactly the same shape as BACKWORD, but for a list of words.
; Compare the two procedures line by line.
to backsentence :sent
  if emptyp :sent [output []]
  output sentence last :sent backsentence butlast :sent
end

; Keep the order of the words but spell each one backwards.
to mirrorwords :sent
  if emptyp :sent [output []]
  output sentence backword first :sent mirrorwords butfirst :sent
end

to showall :sent
  print (sentence [Original:] :sent)
  print (sentence [Words reversed:] backsentence :sent)
  print (sentence [Each word:] mirrorwords :sent)
  ; the full mirror is just the other two ideas combined
  print (sentence [Full mirror:] backsentence mirrorwords :sent)
  print []
end

; Ask for a sentence and show it backwards, over and over.
to askloop
  print [Type a sentence, or quit to stop:]
  localmake "line readlist
  if emptyp :line [print [!eybdooG] stop]
  if equalp :line [quit] [print [!eybdooG] stop]
  showall :line
  askloop
end

showall [the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog]
showall [stressed desserts]
askloop
